      "heading": "A - Exam authority, Basic Driving",
      "learner_facing": true,
      "markdown": "## A - Exam authority, Basic Driving\n\nThis dossier supports first-time never-licensed applicants preparing for the regular passenger-car written knowledge test in Kentucky. The issuing authority is the Kentucky State Police, Driver Testing Branch, and licensing services run through the Transportation Cabinet. Handbook facts in this section come from Section Five of the Kentucky Driver Manual, covering starting the engine, moving, stopping, steering, and backing. The official question count, passing score, test format, and time limit are not stated on the assigned pages, so this dossier asserts no value for any of them. Practice scoring follows only the accepted LearningLoop product policy.\n",
